WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.150
Luxembourg, 2025: 83 per cent of its
goods trade was with other EU countries.

2
00:00:07.200 --> 00:00:10.850
At the other end of the
range is Cyprus: 28 per cent.

3
00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:16.010
Eurostat finds that trade within
the EU dominates for most members.

4
00:00:16.060 --> 00:00:23.310
Exports within the EU rose from 1,500
billion euros in 2002 to peaks above 4,000

5
00:00:23.360 --> 00:00:24.910
billion recently.

6
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:28.390
So why does so much of their
trade stay inside the bloc?

7
00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:31.290
Is it simply that they are neighbours?

8
00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.390
In this mission, you'll climb
a ladder of trade deals,

9
00:00:34.440 --> 00:00:37.290
from loose agreements to deep unions.

10
00:00:37.340 --> 00:00:40.210
Then you'll read the map member by member.

11
00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:45.090
Your mission: explain why most EU
members trade mainly with one another.
